0$ when $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, we can draw the phase line using the following recipe:\n\n- Draw a vertical $y$-axis\n\n- Mark the equilibrium solutions\n\n- Draw arrows pointing up in the intervals where $f(y)>0$\n\n- Draw arrows pointing down in the intervals where $f(y)<0$\n\nApplying the above recipe, we get the following phase line for our differential equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/8073b3575bd48710fe7744221dbebe7f9d0656991ea4a9bea8e11e06431f63d7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317315 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c72cc6e0-deae-51fc-a5e4-b27fcb6f7892" :knowledge-point/title "Phase Lines and Slope Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ae9b70e-87af-5e1c-bda3-797eb6fbb20d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/bbb6defd12fdc683f2df111cce7e10807fd8d69877ddf12de7fa97d3e9d53781.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317317} {:answer/id #uuid "a6766ea0-c2a7-513b-b2b5-79dd127ad727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/daf84f414d35afead0733718b8b50c80f64d326af4aeb94b22356b5e54c9c2ba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317318} {:answer/id #uuid "cc9a5c4b-8eeb-59ee-a97b-ae9c87a10964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/d281794a12395bdbe1a39d23403b59c0d1638820e9951628cf11cedb321dfa0c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317319} {:answer/id #uuid "35fdc2c1-fa8b-5b9d-b5b1-53ee46fe93c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-