\n\n- Draw a vertical $y$-axis\n\n- Mark the equilibrium solutions\n\n- Draw arrows pointing up in the intervals where $f(y)>0$\n\n- Draw arrows pointing down in the intervals where $f(y)<0$\n\nApplying the above recipe, we get the following phase line for our differential equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/bbb6defd12fdc683f2df111cce7e10807fd8d69877ddf12de7fa97d3e9d53781.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c72cc6e0-deae-51fc-a5e4-b27fcb6f7892" :knowledge-point/title "Phase Lines and Slope Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19a1d83a-852f-57ab-8d51-8c5cd24a9e80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/68eff0fb5179ec11111ed4fef03e24df50f8c35c0375ef82a90373cae2f9b246.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317324} {:answer/id #uuid "20cdc014-32f6-52b7-80e2-eefa89c778e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/9a392f874252df611fc92421b98d19f930ac6efe7bd43e82ef2b286cda2b70bc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317325} {:answer/id #uuid "bddbfadf-045b-552e-94e9-718194bfdd24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/40f87baa0460a6efb4e1f1c994edda1b28ddc6e7cfc070535101a7b4b15d7075.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317326} {:answer/id #uuid "a819ce1e-7aa0-5105-acc1-abb867968093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/ec8bc75687dfd235e21144bb73a351392f6eb13c9bf587d751bb8b657994da95.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317327} {:answer/id #uuid "2e077273-62da-5466-9a25-768b9419273d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/7a4a676389d52476b4e17a72bb8a180e3f992aa604ae52a303f53b72d5be5faf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19a1d83a-852f-57ab-8d51-8c5cd24a9e80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/68eff0fb5179ec11111ed4fef03e24df50f8c35c0375ef82a90373cae2f9b246.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317324} :answer-field/id #uuid "c34d7645-e346-50a9-8769-970ee168d980" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c73ad3e7-b3ca-5ad8-bbdd-651ca41243b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-98042" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/d4aac304110ed4743b58ba786141cecc404791130bf35884f8fbefe94c18fbd6.png)\n\nThe phase line of a differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be the slope field of the equation?" :question/worked-solution "From the phase line, we can deduce the following:\n\n- The equilibrium solutions are $y=-2$ and $y=2.$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along these lines.\n\n- $f(y)<0$ for $y\\in (-2,2).$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are negative in this region.\n\n- $f(y)>0$ for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are positive in these regions.\n\nThe only slope field that satisfies the above conditions is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/eb76b700066be49d493fe0738b7c3b18b0b34dcaada93f7c961e5647a0a079c1.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317329 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c72cc6e0-deae-51fc-a5e4-b27fcb6f7892" :knowledge-point/title "Phase Lines and Slope Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dda18b9f-d1e8-5659-9f3f-f0ad044c9adf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/8abe546b96547089599251ce0c45db7e64afe957a50d18ec5d4e734c15cb7954.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317331} {:answer/id #uuid "a46c4afc-7c10-5e9b-9b09-b7b5994fe031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/8a263e4be7a96cfb56230104a72a1495270ca361cfca6d5b602060a9a2318361.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317332} {:answer/id #uuid "984fb1e9-ae3f-5c2e-9d49-ae767fbf14c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/4497b384ad4d9dd3812b6953cc691f5a8f7c3b8e0b8e1d88095af0d9cbefcf96.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317333} {:answer/id #uuid "a909c6d5-0b94-53ae-aa6f-aebd056afbf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/44419413221f356bac454f1aa070e3888a8ea6921db3f7c69033e7b4347f46ec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317334} {:answer/id #uuid "d46a724d-3738-51ca-a15a-8852a808fa6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042698/assets/a99527dcd6429dd699e3ea6bce2a1c9324ff6562791ba333fb3217e12